            <title>[LU-21247] Report NI address removal on the console and clarify the o2ib "consumer defined fatal error" reject</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21247</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When the IP address of an NI is removed or changed while LNet is running (e.g. by NetworkManager), ksocklnd and ko2iblnd mark the NI down but only log it under D_NET. Nothing appears on the console of the node where the address changed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With o2ib, peers that keep connecting to the old address are rejected by the remote RDMA CM, which finds no listener bound to it. The reject carries an all-zero payload, and kiblnd_rejected() logs:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;LNetError: ... 172.16.10.101@o2ib rejected: consumer defined fatal error
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This message is printed on the peers, not on the node where the address changed, and it looks like a hardware or fabric fault. Such cases end up being investigated as network problems, while the cause is an address changed without stopping Lustre/LNet.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Proposal:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;In the inetaddr notifiers of ksocklnd and ko2iblnd, when the event matches the NI address, print on the console: &amp;lt;nid&amp;gt;: address removed from &amp;lt;ifname&amp;gt;, NI unusable until it is restored. If the address was changed, stop Lustre and reconfigure LNet and, when the address comes back: "&amp;lt;nid&amp;gt;: address restored on &amp;lt;ifname&amp;gt;".&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;In kiblnd_rejected(), when the reject payload is all zeros, print: "&amp;lt;nid&amp;gt; rejected: remote host has no LNet NI on this address". Other non-o2iblnd payloads keep the current message.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</description>
